  "_comment": "yaw is the rotation in radians needed to make the model face +Z. All but Finn McMissile face +Z; his model lies along X, hence his yaw of pi/2. Verify with tools/diag_cars.mjs, which renders them textured from the front: these characters have eyes on the windscreen, so the front is unmistakable. An untextured silhouette is not enough - reading one wrong had Chick Hicks racing backwards. length is the real-world length in metres the model is scaled to at load; the raw models range from 5 units to 2005 units so scale is always derived from the bounding box. \"racer\": false marks a model that is in the game but not on the grid: Guido is the pit crew and Mack is parked in the pits. They still load, and the museum still shows them - they are cars, and the showroom is for looking at cars - but Race never builds a Car for them.",
